    {
      "field_name": "diagnostic_criteria",
      "value": "Stiffness and rigidity of the axial musculature; Slow progression of stiffness to include proximal limb muscles, making volitional movements and ambulation difficult; A fixed deformity of the spine (most often hyper-lordosis); The presence of superimposed episodic spasms precipitated by sudden movement, jarring, noise, and emotional upset; Normal findings on motor and sensory examinations; Normal intellect; Electromyographic findings of continuous motor activity abolished by intravenous administration of diazepam",
      "quote": "Criteria to diagnose SPS\n• Stiffness and rigidity of the axial musculature\n• Slow progression of stiffness to include proximal limb muscles, making volitional movements and ambulation difficult\n• A fixed deformity of the spine (most often hyper-lordosis)\n• The presence of superimposed episodic spasms precipitated by sudden movement, jarring, noise, and emotional upset\n• Normal findings on motor and sensory examinations\n• Normal intellect\n• Electromyographic findings of continuous motor activity abolished by intravenous administration of diazepam",
      "confidence": "high"
    },
